        "design_notes": "Fresh Reality Anchor candidate produced by the sokoban design review loop. The accepted v6 version keeps the clean post-prune form: a one-step opening comfort buffer, active sticky L construction through pull and sticky_merge, reuse of that L as a B/S door-sweeping piston, and a final far single target that requires two pull_object strokes with the sticky domino. Prototype pre-submission workflows were executed: invalid_goal_prune removed the v3/v4 top, bottom, and redundant adjacent right target; opening_comfort_check moved the start one cell left; redundant_element_prune found the final v6 clean after those changes. Evidence: shortest cost 13, complete graph with 22 reachable states, 32 legal transitions, and 1 winning state. Core event probe is complete with no winning bypass missing push, pull, sticky rigid movement, B/S shift, force_chain, or sticky_merge. Count probes prove all wins require pull_object >= 5, move_sticky_rigid >= 7, and sticky_merge >= 1. Goal coverage shows target [6,6] is covered only on final step 13. Independent evidence review returned supports_with_caveats / required_action none; puzzle critic returned proposal_ready_with_caveats / required_action none, estimating difficulty as mid 3 and aesthetic as low 4.\n",
